// `<` and `>` on Arrays and Dictionaries used to compare lengths, while `<=`
// and `>=` were not defined on them at all — so four comparison operators meant
// two different things on one type. And the meaning they had is not the one
// they read as: `[1, 2, 3] < [9]` was false, because it asked whether 3 < 1.
println([1, 2, 3] < [9])
